WEBVTT

00:00.680 --> 00:02.480
Thank you for the food!

00:02.480 --> 00:04.820
Fank you for the food!

00:08.410 --> 00:10.400
Mama, tofu!

00:10.400 --> 00:13.050
Okay, coming right up.

00:13.900 --> 00:15.910
Emi, what the heck?!

00:15.910 --> 00:20.090
Alciel, I told you to nix 
the ginger buds on my chilled tofu

00:20.090 --> 00:22.660
because I'd be sharing with Alas Ramus.

00:23.900 --> 00:28.170
Denied. We can't have Alas Ramus 
growing up to be a picky eater.

00:28.170 --> 00:33.110
Still, Mister Ashiya, ginger is 
a little too much for a baby...

00:33.110 --> 00:36.430
I get it. I'm not a ginger bud fan either.

00:36.430 --> 00:39.280
Urushihara, stop complaining like a baby.

00:39.280 --> 00:41.330
Frankly, they're a little much for me, too.

00:41.330 --> 00:42.860
You too, Sire?!

00:42.860 --> 00:44.380
<i>On to our next story.</i>

00:44.380 --> 00:48.370
<i>Fireworks events are planned 
around the country as usual,</i>

00:45.440 --> 00:49.440
<b>Booming! The customary 
fireworks displays around Japan</b>

00:48.370 --> 00:53.070
<i>and many regions are expecting 
larger than average crowds.</i>

00:49.440 --> 00:53.070
A refined custom. 
I'd love to experience one.

00:53.070 --> 00:56.340
Ugh, not me. They're so crowded.

00:56.340 --> 00:58.700
I wouldn't take you there if you begged me.

00:58.700 --> 00:59.840
What? Why?

00:59.840 --> 01:01.700
You know why.

01:04.330 --> 01:05.770
Something wrong?

01:12.540 --> 01:15.970
I'm going to go stay at my 
parents' place for a while.

01:16.530 --> 01:17.540
Huh?

01:39.780 --> 01:41.870
<b>The Devil is a Part-Timer! Season 2</b>

02:51.860 --> 02:54.520
Emilia, about what you said...

02:54.520 --> 02:59.490
m 370 218 l 609 218 609 245 370 245

02:56.110 --> 02:59.490
<b>The Hero Says Good-Bye for a Time</b>

02:56.110 --> 02:59.490
<b>The Hero Says Good-Bye for a Time</b>

02:57.960 --> 03:00.530
I'm sick of waiting.

03:01.950 --> 03:05.030
My goal was to defeat the Devil.

03:05.600 --> 03:10.540
But then there was Alas Ramus, 
and defeating him got complicated,

03:10.540 --> 03:13.300
and now there are angels 
and demons and whatnot

03:13.300 --> 03:15.790
coming after us and stirring 
up trouble, you know?

03:17.050 --> 03:22.050
I'm fed up with random 
outsiders messing with me.

03:22.700 --> 03:25.880
That's why I decided to go 
back to Ente Isla for a while.

03:26.370 --> 03:30.420
If I retrace Lailah's—my 
mother's—footsteps in Ente Isla,

03:30.420 --> 03:32.730
I might figure things out a little.

03:32.730 --> 03:35.940
You think Lailah may hold the secret.

03:35.940 --> 03:38.950
Yeah. The sacred sword, the Yesod shards,

03:38.950 --> 03:41.320
the connection between 
Heaven and the demons...

03:41.320 --> 03:44.700
I'm not counting on finding a clue,
 but maybe I'll get lucky.

03:45.470 --> 03:48.330
Um, is it okay if I see you off?

03:48.580 --> 03:54.700
I'm sorry, but Emerada is opening 
the Gate for me this Monday afternoon.

03:54.700 --> 03:56.420
You'll be in school.

03:57.340 --> 04:00.380
I'll see her off, good Chiho.

04:01.700 --> 04:06.850
It's okay, Chiho. I'll be back 
no later than the 12th.

04:07.450 --> 04:10.600
The 12th... Oh, right.

04:10.640 --> 04:19.110
<b>Joint birthday party!
 Happy birthday to Miss Yusa, too</b>

04:11.410 --> 04:13.850
That's your joint birthday party with Chi.

04:13.850 --> 04:18.680
Ah, yes. Your birthday is in 
the autumn by this world's calendar.

04:24.000 --> 04:28.580
Don't worry. I <i>am</i> history's 
strongest hero, you know.

04:28.580 --> 04:31.510
I wouldn't do anything dangerous 
with Alas Ramus there,

04:31.510 --> 04:34.000
and I'm basically just going 
to clean up my old home.

04:34.470 --> 04:36.250
I'll be back soon.

04:36.250 --> 04:38.800
Right, of course.

04:38.800 --> 04:41.860
I'll practice my "kids' curry"

04:41.860 --> 04:44.380
so I'm good at it for Alas Ramus 
before you get back.

04:44.700 --> 04:49.390
'urry? Where's 'urry...?

04:49.390 --> 04:51.400
Oh, you're awake.

04:51.400 --> 04:54.140
Let's beddy-bye at home, okay?

04:56.790 --> 04:59.200
See you next week, Chiho.

04:59.200 --> 05:00.880
I'll message you later, Bel.

05:00.880 --> 05:02.150
Bye-bye!

05:02.150 --> 05:06.780
Papa, Chi-sis, Suzu-sis, bye-bye!

05:09.390 --> 05:10.160
I'm home.

05:10.160 --> 05:12.190
Welcome back, Sire!

05:12.690 --> 05:14.740
Wow, you're sure in good spirits.

05:14.740 --> 05:19.420
I'm just glad to be rid 
of Emilia for a while!

05:19.540 --> 05:19.590
<b>OFF</b>

05:19.590 --> 05:19.630
<b>OFF</b>

05:19.630 --> 05:19.670
<b>OFF</b>

05:19.670 --> 05:19.710
<b>OFF</b>

05:19.710 --> 05:20.540
<b>OFF</b>

05:20.570 --> 05:23.530
Thank goodness I saved this 
for just such an occasion!

05:23.530 --> 05:27.050
Let's go eat some grilled organ meats!

05:27.050 --> 05:31.560
Oh hey, did you see my message 
asking you to bring home some flan?

05:31.560 --> 05:32.650
No.

05:33.060 --> 05:37.560
Aw, but Ashiya okayed it for once!

05:40.560 --> 05:41.760
Sire?

05:41.760 --> 05:43.820
Maou? What's wrong?

05:43.820 --> 05:46.570
You want yakiniku and flan 
while the hero is away?!

05:46.570 --> 05:49.570
Do you realize Emi basically trusts us?!

05:49.570 --> 05:53.000
Have some pride as demon generals!

05:53.000 --> 05:55.700
Enough stupid fights! 
You're annoying your neighbors!

06:02.590 --> 06:05.590
<b>September 6th</b>

06:02.590 --> 06:05.590
<b>Monday</b>

06:03.980 --> 06:05.590
It's time.

06:11.230 --> 06:16.700
I thought this might react when 
Miss Yusa passed through a Gate...

06:28.360 --> 06:31.370
<b></b>From:  <b>Miss Suzuno</b>

06:28.360 --> 06:31.370
<b></b>To:  <b>Me</b>

06:28.360 --> 06:31.370
<b></b>Date:  9/6 12:16

06:28.360 --> 06:31.370
<b></b>Emilia's safe. She departed with Emerada.

06:36.880 --> 06:42.380
I hope Ente Isla is as peaceful 
as possible when Miss Yusa gets there.

06:42.420 --> 06:45.340
<b>September 7th</b>

06:45.420 --> 06:48.340
<b>September 8th</b>

06:48.420 --> 06:51.340
<b>September 9th</b>

06:51.430 --> 06:54.350
<b>September 10th</b>

06:58.390 --> 07:00.390
<b>Moped License Practice Test</b>

06:58.390 --> 07:00.390
<b>Problem 6       (True or False)</b>

06:58.390 --> 07:00.390
<b>You must always stop at red lights</b>

07:05.410 --> 07:08.850
Your Majesty, I think you 
could use a break from studying.

07:08.850 --> 07:10.310
Right, sorry.

07:10.940 --> 07:15.410
Can't believe the Devil wants 
the government's permission for something.

07:15.410 --> 07:17.410
Let alone to drive a <i>moped</i>.

07:17.800 --> 07:21.480
How dare you?! Don't discourage 
His Majesty's efforts!

07:21.950 --> 07:25.000
Anyway, it's not like 
you need to get a license

07:25.000 --> 07:27.560
just because MgRonald's 
wants to start delivering.

07:27.560 --> 07:29.490
You'll just end up with more work.

07:29.490 --> 07:32.890
I'm assigned as shift manager 
more often lately.

07:32.890 --> 07:35.410
I need to be ready to cover for any absences,

07:35.410 --> 07:37.110
so I want my license in advance.

07:37.110 --> 07:39.680
You're so admirable, Sire!

07:39.680 --> 07:43.470
That's not really what this is about.

07:44.560 --> 07:46.570
<b>Joint birthday party!
 Happy birthday to Miss Yusa, too</b>

07:49.390 --> 07:51.820
Emilia doesn't seem to be back yet.

07:53.430 --> 07:54.750
Yeah...

08:09.320 --> 08:13.230
Excuse me. Has Emilia come back yet?

08:13.640 --> 08:15.450
You mean she hasn't?

08:15.970 --> 08:21.600
She hasn't contacted me, but I thought
 perhaps she'd contacted you...

08:21.600 --> 08:24.920
If you and Chi don't know, I certainly don't.

08:24.920 --> 08:27.730
Why don't you try contacting Emerada?

08:27.730 --> 08:30.360
She's not answering me, either.

08:31.610 --> 08:35.070
The situation in Ente Isla 
is complicated right now.

08:35.440 --> 08:37.370
We can't send too many idea links,

08:37.370 --> 08:39.870
because the wrong person might detect them.

08:39.870 --> 08:42.620
Yeah, Olba's just one example.

08:42.620 --> 08:46.030
But if something bad has happened...

08:46.030 --> 08:49.140
The kind of incident that 
would cause radio silence

08:49.140 --> 08:53.000
from the same Hero who can beat 
back Devil's armies and archangels

08:53.000 --> 08:54.130
would surely be apocalyptic.

08:54.980 --> 08:58.510
You can open Gates when you 
have your magic, right, Maou?

08:58.930 --> 09:03.390
So why not let yourself get 
overloaded with celestial force again

09:03.390 --> 09:05.520
and get your magic back?

09:05.520 --> 09:08.910
And then go check out Ente Isla?

09:08.910 --> 09:10.520
I probably can't.

09:10.930 --> 09:17.340
Satan is right. I'm not sure I have 
even half of Emilia's power.

09:17.340 --> 09:19.530
It's not enough to overload him.

09:19.530 --> 09:23.540
Aw, man... I thought it was a good idea.

09:23.540 --> 09:24.800
Hold up.

09:25.470 --> 09:28.090
Is it me, or you all acting like 
Emi's definitely in trouble—

09:28.090 --> 09:31.300
and like <i>I</i> have to go save her?

09:31.840 --> 09:34.930
I'm her enemy, you know! 
King of demons, remember?

09:34.930 --> 09:38.650
I don't care what the humans 
in Ente Isla are doing.

09:38.650 --> 09:41.810
In fact, if they kill each other 
in a war, that's to my advantage.

09:42.390 --> 09:47.010
Even if Emi <i>is</i> in trouble, 
I can't do anything about it,

09:47.010 --> 09:49.440
and there's no need for me to care anyway.

09:49.440 --> 09:51.570
But Satan...

09:53.330 --> 09:55.090
Conversation over.

09:55.090 --> 09:57.990
Today's party'll be canceled 
if Emi doesn't come, right?

09:58.830 --> 10:01.580
I take my moped license test tomorrow.

10:02.990 --> 10:07.830
Satan, would you say the same 
thing if Chiho asked for help?

10:10.570 --> 10:14.330
I'd word it more gently, but my
 conclusion wouldn't change.

10:15.080 --> 10:16.510
Mister Maou.

10:21.350 --> 10:22.830
M-Miss Sasaki...

10:22.830 --> 10:25.160
Talk about underhanded.

10:25.160 --> 10:26.350
Chi...

10:26.920 --> 10:31.980
Mister Maou, I know that you're not 
the kind of person to break promises.

10:33.360 --> 10:40.740
Remember what you said? 
Remember your wonderful present?

10:41.240 --> 10:47.130
You said that me, Miss Suzuno, 
and Miss Yusa were your generals.

10:47.130 --> 10:51.090
You promised to show us a new 
world if we were by your side.

10:51.090 --> 10:52.500
Miss Sasaki...

10:52.500 --> 10:55.990
Alas Ramus is with her, you know.

10:55.990 --> 10:59.670
There's no way you aren't worried.

11:00.040 --> 11:03.890
So you're lying right now, Mister Maou.

11:04.380 --> 11:05.890
Chiho...

11:06.610 --> 11:11.350
I'm the one who asked 
Miss Suzuno to check with you.

11:11.750 --> 11:14.400
Sorry for tricking you!

11:18.040 --> 11:22.710
I'll try to think of something 
I can do. Excuse me.

11:30.160 --> 11:31.300
Shit!

11:34.270 --> 11:36.680
If I may, Your Majesty...

11:36.680 --> 11:40.800
You wanna tell me to worry about Emi, too?

11:40.800 --> 11:45.500
No, I believe we face 
graver matters right now.

11:46.680 --> 11:51.000
Even our Devil's army wasn't able 
to best Emilia in a fair fight.

11:51.000 --> 11:55.750
But if humans are warring 
with humans in Ente Isla,

11:55.750 --> 12:01.700
you know any threat to Emilia 
won't necessarily be fighting fair.

12:02.210 --> 12:05.150
In addition to the Church 
and the other authorities,

12:05.150 --> 12:08.450
the Malebranche and even Heaven 
itself are her enemies now.

12:09.330 --> 12:14.050
If any of them have somehow found 
out that Emilia is in Ente Isla,

12:14.620 --> 12:16.710
I doubt they'll let it pass.

12:16.710 --> 12:20.180
They couldn't beat Emi with strength... but...

12:21.730 --> 12:26.090
You think there are hostages? That 
Emerada may have been taken hostage?

12:26.090 --> 12:30.970
It needn't be Emerada Etuva. 
Anyone Emilia cares for would do.

12:31.600 --> 12:36.200
Anyone who would make her hold back.

12:36.200 --> 12:40.520
But why would Ente Islans go that far?

12:41.030 --> 12:43.240
She's the hero that saved their world.

12:45.180 --> 12:47.460
I believe naming Emilia 
and Bel your generals

12:47.460 --> 12:52.870
when you sent Farfarello 
home was unwise, Sire.

12:52.870 --> 12:55.980
I got carried away in the moment, sure,

12:56.300 --> 12:58.300
but I did it to protect Chi

12:58.300 --> 13:02.060
and keep more demons from 
showing up in Japan, you know?

13:06.510 --> 13:08.620
Oh, I get it!

13:08.620 --> 13:10.900
Will the humans there get mad

13:10.900 --> 13:13.130
because they think Emi 
and Suzuno betrayed them?!

13:13.860 --> 13:16.060
They may not believe that right away,

13:16.060 --> 13:19.020
but someone who harbored 
doubt might make a move.

13:19.020 --> 13:21.620
And Emi and Suzuno knew that?

13:21.620 --> 13:27.030
I assume they willingly took 
on the danger for Miss Sasaki's sake.

13:27.340 --> 13:29.370
Didn't Emilia herself indicate

13:29.370 --> 13:32.540
that she went home because 
she was tired of playing defense?

13:33.150 --> 13:38.040
In their own way, I believe she and Bel 
want to protect our status quo.

13:38.860 --> 13:40.890
They want to protect this lifestyle

13:40.890 --> 13:44.180
where as incompatible and 
prone to bickering as we are,

13:44.180 --> 13:45.550
we sit at the same table.

13:45.970 --> 13:49.990
Where did I put that thing? I know 
I left it here last time I came.

13:49.990 --> 13:52.350
Urushihara, what are you messing about for?!

13:52.350 --> 13:54.180
We're having a serious discussion!

13:54.180 --> 13:57.310
Ignore him. Keep going, Ashiya.

13:57.310 --> 14:02.370
Yes, Sire! A normal human 
couldn't match Emilia in a fight.

14:02.370 --> 14:06.700
However, certain forces value Emilia 
for more than her battle prowess.

14:08.490 --> 14:09.490
The angels?

14:10.200 --> 14:12.300
That's all just speculation.

14:12.300 --> 14:16.860
Ente Isla's not like Japan, 
where the trains come on schedule.

14:16.860 --> 14:18.960
She's probably just running late.

14:18.960 --> 14:21.500
That sounds overly optimistic.

14:21.500 --> 14:24.040
Plus, even if they <i>are</i> holding a hostage,

14:24.040 --> 14:29.790
I don't think anyone on Earth or Ente Isla 
now could straight-up kill Emilia.

14:30.110 --> 14:33.470
As long as Emilia's alive, 
Alas Ramus should be fine, too.

14:34.300 --> 14:38.480
And even if she's in trouble, 
it's not like she'd want your help.

14:40.970 --> 14:42.730
Ashiya. Urushihara.

14:42.730 --> 14:43.730
Sire!

14:43.730 --> 14:44.730
Hmm?

14:45.200 --> 14:49.800
Thanks. I feel a little calmer 
after what you two said.

14:49.800 --> 14:51.990
For now I'll concentrate 
on what's in front of me.

14:52.680 --> 14:56.800
When she comes back, I'm gonna 
mock her like hell for being late

14:56.800 --> 14:58.600
and rub my license in her face.

14:59.850 --> 15:02.000
May you return victorious, Sire.

15:02.000 --> 15:05.070
That's a little much. 
It's just a moped license.

15:05.070 --> 15:06.070
Oops!

15:05.710 --> 15:08.260
Moped License
Practice Test Questions

15:08.750 --> 15:11.260
Okay, I guess I'm a little nervous.

15:11.260 --> 15:14.080
A little nervousness is good.

15:14.560 --> 15:18.770
I'm sure you'll pass the test 
despite all difficulties.

15:18.770 --> 15:20.330
See you later, then.

15:27.780 --> 15:29.280
<b>September 27
Monday</b>

15:27.780 --> 15:30.770
<i>This is Tenmondai-mae.</i>

15:33.650 --> 15:35.300
Made it in time!

15:35.300 --> 15:37.540
Hurry, Dad!

15:51.570 --> 15:52.800
H-Hey!

15:53.460 --> 15:55.180
I'm so sorry, sir.

15:55.180 --> 15:56.860
<i>Foreigners?</i>

15:56.860 --> 15:59.180
You apologize too, Tsubasa.

15:59.180 --> 16:01.020
Will do, Dad!

16:01.020 --> 16:02.190
Sorry!

16:12.940 --> 16:15.860
<i>Next stop, Shikenjo-Seimon.</i>

16:15.860 --> 16:21.580
<i>Exit here for Driver's License Headquarters, 
Fuchu Driver's License Center.</i>

16:17.710 --> 16:19.120
B-Bye!

16:25.080 --> 16:27.980
All right, these should be dry by afternoon.

16:30.070 --> 16:31.250
Miss Suzuki?

16:31.590 --> 16:33.590
<b>Driver's License Headquarters • Fuchu Driver's License Center</b>

16:33.960 --> 16:36.590
Looks like there's time left before my turn.

16:40.820 --> 16:42.680
You're here for a license, too?

16:43.670 --> 16:45.710
How many times have you tested?

16:45.710 --> 16:49.730
This is me and Dad's tenth time! Memorial!

16:49.730 --> 16:52.850
Tenth?! Uh, this is my first...

16:52.850 --> 16:58.740
Dad can't read kanji good yet. 
I came as his companion.

16:59.720 --> 17:00.960
I see...

17:00.960 --> 17:03.330
I didn't study, though!

17:03.910 --> 17:05.380
Well, good luck.

17:06.750 --> 17:08.750
What's your name?

17:09.490 --> 17:11.130
Um...

17:11.130 --> 17:14.510
I'm A—nope, I'm Tsubasa Satou.

17:16.090 --> 17:18.510
Dad is Hiroshi Satou!

17:19.030 --> 17:22.270
Right, okay, I'm Maou.

17:22.270 --> 17:25.020
Are you like a king of demons?

17:32.030 --> 17:35.150
"Maou" sounds like 
the final boss in a video game!

17:36.520 --> 17:37.910
Nope, not me.

17:41.660 --> 17:44.160
What the hell is with you guys?!

17:44.160 --> 17:47.280
Tsubasa, you shouldn't 
do things that stand out.

17:47.280 --> 17:50.670
But he smelled so familiar.

17:51.320 --> 17:55.250
Like a warm place I was in
a long time ago...

17:56.670 --> 17:58.680
<b>Shiro Ashiya</b>

18:07.330 --> 18:08.440
Here's some tea.

18:08.440 --> 18:10.460
Oh, thank you.

18:10.460 --> 18:12.940
How did you know where our apartment is?

18:12.940 --> 18:17.130
I exchanged contact info with Suzuno 
when we went TV shopping.

18:17.130 --> 18:21.720
I felt bad about visiting you 
without asking first...

18:22.150 --> 18:24.950
But I had to do something.

18:25.910 --> 18:27.710
This is about Yusa, isn't it?

18:27.710 --> 18:31.960
Yeah. Have you heard from Emi?

18:32.490 --> 18:36.590
We can't get through on the phone, 
and none of our messages to her say "Read."

18:36.590 --> 18:38.600
I went to her place, but she's out.

18:38.600 --> 18:42.530
And she's been absent 
without leave for a long time.

18:42.970 --> 18:46.340
Emi lives alone, and her 
parents are abroad, right?

18:46.340 --> 18:47.850
Y-Yes.

18:47.850 --> 18:50.230
She said she had family business,

18:50.230 --> 18:54.010
but since she doesn't seem to 
have friends outside of work,

18:54.010 --> 18:56.780
we're all worried that 
if she's really sick or injured,

18:56.780 --> 19:00.360
we might never know.

19:00.920 --> 19:05.620
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid we 
don't know any more than you do.

19:05.620 --> 19:08.940
Maybe I should contact the police.

19:08.940 --> 19:12.790
It's weird for her to be 
out of contact for a week!

19:13.730 --> 19:16.480
What was that, Miss Suzuki?

19:16.480 --> 19:18.240
How long has it been since you talked?

19:18.240 --> 19:20.620
I told you, it's been a week.

19:20.620 --> 19:26.770
W-Wait a minute. When did you 
last hear from Emil—Emi?

19:26.770 --> 19:29.370
Last Friday night.

19:29.370 --> 19:34.140
We lost touch with her 
the Friday before last.

19:34.140 --> 19:37.780
Well, no, that's when she said she'd be back.

19:37.780 --> 19:39.900
So really, it's been three weeks.

19:37.780 --> 19:40.900
<b>Joint birthday party!
 Happy birthday to Miss Yusa, too</b>

19:37.780 --> 19:40.900
<b>His Majesty's driving test</b>

19:39.900 --> 19:40.900
What?!

19:40.900 --> 19:42.540
Was it a phone call?

19:42.540 --> 19:45.310
Yeah, it was. One sec.

19:45.910 --> 19:48.790
<b>Yumi
Maki
Mama
Unknown Number</b>

19:46.730 --> 19:48.420
Unknown number?

19:48.790 --> 19:52.040
Could it have been someone 
pretending to be Emi?

19:52.040 --> 19:54.710
Definitely not. It was Emi's voice,

19:54.710 --> 19:57.930
and she said her name 
before I said anything.

19:57.930 --> 20:00.410
She sounded the same as always, too.

20:00.410 --> 20:04.180
Forgive my prying, but what 
did you speak with her about?

20:05.040 --> 20:08.180
She wanted to swap shifts with me...

20:12.960 --> 20:13.890
Huh?

20:13.890 --> 20:15.310
What is it?

20:15.310 --> 20:18.410
It was so sunny just a minute ago...

20:18.410 --> 20:21.210
Didn't the forecast say it 
wouldn't rain until afternoon?

20:22.700 --> 20:24.820
Was anything else unusual at all?

20:25.530 --> 20:28.540
I think she sounded a little far away.

20:28.540 --> 20:33.370
And her voice was kind of breathy... 
And she talked faster than usual.

20:33.370 --> 20:37.840
But I figured she might be overseas, 
so I didn't think too much of it.

20:37.840 --> 20:40.250
Why choose Rika?

20:40.250 --> 20:41.080
Huh?

20:43.100 --> 20:45.720
Sorry, it seems to be raining.

20:45.720 --> 20:49.000
Oh, dear. I left my window open.

20:49.000 --> 20:50.100
Pardon me.

20:50.100 --> 20:52.390
Urushihara, you help too.

20:52.390 --> 20:53.660
Okay.

20:58.980 --> 21:02.550
Hey, Urushihara! There's a lady present!

21:02.860 --> 21:06.150
It's okay. Please don't worry.

21:06.150 --> 21:08.700
Whoa, look at that sky.

21:08.700 --> 21:11.260
I don't think the weather report 
predicted <i>that</i> much rain.

21:12.230 --> 21:13.370
We have an emergency!

21:13.370 --> 21:14.620
Wh-What?!

21:14.620 --> 21:15.870
Lucifer.

21:17.000 --> 21:18.040
Isn't this...

21:18.380 --> 21:20.880
<b>Holyvitan β</b>

21:18.840 --> 21:20.160
what you two use?

21:20.880 --> 21:22.880
<b>Receiving</b>

21:20.880 --> 21:22.880
<b>Press to accept call</b>

21:20.880 --> 21:22.880
<b>Unknown Number</b>

21:20.880 --> 21:22.880
It's an SOS from Chiho.

21:22.880 --> 21:25.260
An idea link from Miss Sasaki?

21:25.260 --> 21:28.930
Lucifer, you're our only 
option right now. Let's fly.

21:28.930 --> 21:30.760
She's at her school.

21:31.950 --> 21:32.970
Yeah, yeah.

21:33.450 --> 21:37.770
Chiho Sasaki's school is 
Sasahata North High School, right?

21:37.770 --> 21:40.540
Chiho? The Chiho I know?

21:40.540 --> 21:42.530
H-Hey, Kamazuki! What's happening?!

21:42.530 --> 21:45.340
I'm sorry, good Rika. I'll explain later.

21:45.340 --> 21:47.470
We have no time to waste.

21:47.470 --> 21:51.810
The damage could extend past her 
to her school and its surroundings.

21:58.290 --> 21:59.840
Divine Boots of Light!

22:07.050 --> 22:08.980
<i>Huh</i>?!
